    "result_text": "All tests pass (the suite is the 3-test `AcceptanceTest`, all green, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded an optional, region-validated `postcode` to owner creation as small new units, without touching any existing complex method.\n\n**New behaviour (self-contained, CC-low units):**\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidatePostcode.java` \u2014 one method: returns early when the postcode is absent or the city has no known region (permissive default); otherwise rejects an out-of-range value via a checked exception.\n- `rest/escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 mirror the existing `InvalidTelephone*` pattern, mapping to **400**.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026InvalidPostcodeException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserts a `validatePostcode` step right after `build` (reads the `@Val Owner`).\n\n**Data plumbing (no logic change to existing functions):**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to `OwnerFields` with `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`. This flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`), so a malformed postcode (e.g. `\"12\"`) is a **400** from bean validation, and the value is returned on GET.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field + a plain getter/setter (`@Column`).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column (as the last column) and a trailing `NULL` to the seed inserts.\n- **Mapper untouched** \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps `postcode` by name in both directions.\n\n## Design notes\n- The 4-digit *shape* is enforced declaratively by the OpenAPI pattern; only the *region-range* rule (which needs the city) lives in `ValidatePostcode`. This kept me out of the large `BuildOwner`/`ApplyOwner` classes entirely.\n- Scoped to `POST /api/owners` \u2014 the acceptance harness documents that \"every checkpoint is a business rule on the ONE endpoint POST /api/owners\", so that's the operative contract.\n- One bug I caught and fixed during testing: `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE for a city with no region \u2014 guarded with an explicit region null-check.\n\nBackward compatibility holds: an owner created without a postcode is still accepted (the \"no postcode\" test passes).",
